    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29663" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσώνῠμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearing an ill name,
				hateful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υἷες Ἀχαιῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.255
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.571
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοῖρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.116
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέκτρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					528
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					403
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.258
				</span></i>
			; esp. <i>bearing a name of ill omen</i>, such as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴας</span>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				914
			</span></i> (lyr.): 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.680
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				88.9
			</span></i> (lyr.) perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. γλώσσῃ</span>
			<i>whose</i> tongue <i>earned him an ill name</i> (of
			Thersites).</div>
